        body: 'Dairy hides under a dozen names — whey, casein, milk solids, lactose, butterfat — and it turns up where you\'d never look: sandwich bread, salad dressing, deli meat, protein bars. If your strategy is checking every ingredient list, you\'ll be doing it forever, and you\'ll still get caught by products that quietly change their recipe. The calmer strategy flips the problem. Instead of auditing everything you might eat, build your week around meals you already know are dairy-free or low-lactose. When the default is safe, label-checking becomes the exception — something you do for the occasional new product, not a ritual before every bite. That shift, from defense to planning, is what separates people who manage lactose intolerance comfortably from people who dread every meal.',
